description: Console trust boundaries and security defaults
alwaysApply: true
---

# What this is
A scan console. Users submit a git URL or image ref. Tools are Semgrep, Checkov, Trivy, and SonarQube. Stack is Flask, Postgres, PyJWT, Argon2, Docker SDK, Compose, HTML templates, and a secondary React/Vite UI.

# Trust boundaries
- Repo URL, image ref, branch, commit, and every file inside a clone are untrusted.
- The console process never receives the Docker socket. Only the scanner worker does, and it accepts only approved jobs over a shared token.
- Scan containers use pinned images. A user image is a Trivy argument. It is never the container image that runs.
- Secrets come from env or Docker secret files. Never hardcode them. Never log passwords, tokens, JWTs, or Authorization headers.
- Fail closed. Generic errors to the client. Details only in server logs.
- Do not add a dependency to satisfy a checklist. Match the controls already in this repo.
- Forbidden on untrusted data: eval, exec, pickle, yaml.load, shell=True.
- A change to login, authorization, valid_repo, or valid_image_ref needs a negative test.

# When changing code
Preserve the split between console and scanner. Do not mount docker.sock on the console. Do not weaken SSRF checks in repos.py and images.py to make a scan succeed.
